# Silver Sable, Mercenary Leader: a creature that is equipped is modified (CR 700.9) though it has no counter. Bot1 equips its
# Ornithopter with Lavaspur Boots on turn 1. On turn 3 Sable's enters trigger puts its counter on Bot2's Ornithopter, which is then a
# modified creature but not one Bot1 controls. When Sable attacks, the one modified creature Bot1 controls is its equipped Ornithopter,
# the one target, and it gains lifelink; Sable herself, unmodified, does not.

[Bot1 Deck]
Silver Sable, Mercenary Leader
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Ornithopter
Lavaspur Boots
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lavaspur Boots.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Lavaspur Boots.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Silver Sable, Mercenary Leader.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Attack(Silver Sable, Mercenary Leader > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying; Haste; Lifelink
Bot1.Battlefield.Silver Sable, Mercenary Leader.Keywords = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
